    "engine": "knitr",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"A Long-term Observatory on the Seafloor\"\nmenutitle: \"Benthic Lander Observatory System\"\npage_editors:\n  - name: Hauke Pape\n  - name: Zhehao Hu\n---\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n\n\nBLOS, stands for **Benthic Lander Observatory System**, is a customized system designed for data collection on the seafloor for a long period of time. Currently, three of such systems have been successfully deployed around Iceland during the MSM145 expedition in 2026. \n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div id=\"htmlwidget-8094806e7abc0c89e90c\" style=\"width:100%;height:480px;\" class=\"leaflet html-widget\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-8094806e7abc0c89e90c\">{\"x\":{\"options\":{\"crs\":{\"crsClass\":\"L.CRS.EPSG3857\",\"code\":null,\"proj4def\":null,\"projectedBounds\":null,\"options\":{}}},\"calls\":[{\"method\":\"addProviderTiles\",\"args\":[\"Esri.OceanBasemap\",null,null,{\"errorTileUrl\":\"\",\"noWrap\":false,\"detectRetina\":false}]},{\"method\":\"addMarkers\",\"args\":[[63.30466,63.88253,66.60413],[-16.87085,-13.9806,-17.653983],null,null,null,{\"interactive\":true,\"draggable\":false,\"keyboard\":true,\"title\":\"\",\"alt\":\"\",\"zIndexOffset\":0,\"opacity\":1,\"riseOnHover\":false,\"riseOffset\":250},[\"<div style='text-align:center;'><img src='../../assets/img/blos_infrontof_artreef.webp' width='250px'><br><b>Artificial Reef<\\/b><br>Six artificial coral reefs are dropped to the seafloor in collaboration with the HFRI from Iceland. The BLOS is monitoring one of them.<\\/div>\",\"<div style='text-align:center;'><img src='../../assets/img/blos_infrontof_coralreef.webp' width='250px'><br><b>Cold Water Coral Reef<\\/b><br>An intact, lively cold-water coral reef is chosen as a comparison to the artificial reef site.<\\/div>\",\"<div style='text-align:center;'><img src='../../assets/img/blos_infrontof_vent.webp' width='250px'><br><b>Hydrothermal Vent<\\/b><br>As delicate and vulnerable marine habitats, hydrothermal vents are on the top list as our BLOS target.<\\/div>\"],null,null,null,null,{\"interactive\":false,\"permanent\":false,\"direction\":\"auto\",\"opacity\":1,\"offset\":[0,0],\"textsize\":\"10px\",\"textOnly\":false,\"className\":\"\",\"sticky\":true},null]}],\"limits\":{\"lat\":[63.30466,66.60413],\"lng\":[-17.653983,-13.9806]}},\"evals\":[],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n\n\nDeployed BLOS around Iceland - they are recording the seafloor as you look at this!\n:::\n:::\n\n\n\n\n## How are they built?\n\nThe conceptual design of our BLOS is based on the landers originally constructed by [IFREMER](https://www.ifremer.fr/fr). The physical structure consists of stainless steel frames to mount the individual components, including the camera, energy modules, the communication and storage systems. To ensure stable deployment and long-term durability in the extreme deep-sea environment, the equipment housings are constructed from titanium, a material known for its high resistance to immense pressure and saltwater corrosion. Once deployed, the system operates autonomously, programmed to record between 60 and 160 seconds of video every 12 hours. This continuous monitoring cycle will be carried out for an entire year until the next visit to retrieve the data. \n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<figure id=\"roulette-blos-1\" class=\"roulette-container\" style=\"margin: 0; padding: 0;\" data-images=\"[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Our engineers Maik (left) and Hauke (right) assemblying BLOS onboard&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/maik_hauke_blos.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Our engineers Maik (left) and Hauke (right) assemblying BLOS onboard&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;BLOS testing its lighting configuration in front of an artificial coral reef&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/blos_infrontof_artreef.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;BLOS testing its lighting configuration in front of an artificial coral reef&quot;}]\">\n<div class=\"roulette-stage\" style=\"height: 400px; position: relative; width: 100%; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; overflow: hidden; box-sizing: border-box;\"></div>\n<a href=\"../../assets/img/maik_hauke_blos.webp\" class=\"lightbox\" style=\"display: none;\">dummy</a>\n<div class=\"roulette-thumbnails\" style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center;\">\n<div class=\"r-track\"></div>\n</div>\n<figcaption class=\"roulette-caption\" style=\"text-align: center; margin-top: 10px; width: 100%;\">\n<div class=\"caption-text\" style=\"text-align: center; margin: 0 auto;\">Our engineers Maik (left) and Hauke (right) assemblying BLOS onboard</div>\n</figcaption>\n</figure>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n\n\n## Deployment and Recovery\n\nOur BLOS are specifically designed for deployment and recovery using [GEOMAR's _ROV Phoca_](https://www.geomar.de/en/st/tlz/rovphoca/overview), allowing the entire system to be loaded onto the ROV's porch in one go and brought to the desired spot on the seafloor. To set up the systems efficiently, we use deep-sea Wi-Fi modules developed by IFREMER. \n\nThe ROV and the BLOS each hold a Wi-Fi module that allows real-time data transmission from the BLOS computer to the ROV. Once the ROV reaches the deployment site, the positioning, lighting, and camera configuration are carried out by controlling the BLOS directly from the mission control onboard the vessel. When all settings are complete, the Wi-Fi module linking the BLOS is removed from the ROV container, detaching the two systems completely.\n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<figure id=\"roulette-blos-2\" class=\"roulette-container\" style=\"margin: 0; padding: 0;\" data-images=\"[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;BLOS loaded on _ROV Phoca_&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/blos_on_rov.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;BLOS loaded on &lt;em&gt;ROV Phoca&lt;\\/em&gt;&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;_ROV Phoca_ being deployed with the BLOS on its porch&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/phoca_deployment.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&lt;em&gt;ROV Phoca&lt;\\/em&gt; being deployed with the BLOS on its porch&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Scientists sitting in the mission control to watch the deployment of BLOS&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/confroom.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Scientists sitting in the mission control to watch the deployment of BLOS&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Wi-Fi module visible from side view of the ROV&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/wifi_rov.jpg&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Wi-Fi module visible from side view of the ROV&quot;}]\">\n<div class=\"roulette-stage\" style=\"height: 400px; position: relative; width: 100%; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; overflow: hidden; box-sizing: border-box;\"></div>\n<a href=\"../../assets/img/blos_on_rov.webp\" class=\"lightbox\" style=\"display: none;\">dummy</a>\n<div class=\"roulette-thumbnails\" style=\"\">\n<div class=\"r-track\"></div>\n</div>\n<figcaption class=\"roulette-caption\" style=\"text-align: center; margin-top: 10px; width: 100%;\">\n<div class=\"caption-text\" style=\"text-align: center; margin: 0 auto;\">BLOS loaded on <em>ROV Phoca</em></div>\n</figcaption>\n</figure>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n<hr>\n\n**Editor:** Hauke Pape, Zhehao Hu \n\n[&#8592; Back](../../index.qmd){.btn .btn-outline-primary role='button'}\n",
